From: HaeImAlan <me@haeimalan.com>
Date: Sun, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: rawnand: qcom_nandc: always scan serial NAND with the 2k ID table

qcom_nandc only consults qspinand_flash_ids_2k[] when nandc->boot_layout
is set. That flag is a runtime sysfs toggle which defaults to false and
is never set before probe, so on a normal boot the serial-NAND path falls
through to nand_scan(), which searches the generic nand_flash_ids[] table
instead -- where this SoC's serial parts are not listed at all. The
vendor's own ID table is therefore unreachable in exactly the case it
exists for.

Always scan with the serial table on the serial-NAND path.

Note this is the 5.4 fork's shape of the problem only. The 4.4 fork
defines nand_flash_ids[] inside qcom_nandc.c and reaches it via plain
nand_scan(), so it needs the ID entry alone and no control-flow change.

--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/qcom_nandc.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/qcom_nandc.c
@@ -3787,10 +3787,7 @@
 
 	if (nandc->props->is_serial_nand) {
 		qspi_nand_init(nandc);
-		if (nandc->boot_layout)
-			ret = nand_scan_with_ids(chip, 1, qspinand_flash_ids_2k);
-		else
-			ret = nand_scan(chip, 1);
+		ret = nand_scan_with_ids(chip, 1, qspinand_flash_ids_2k);
 	} else {
 		ret = nand_scan(chip, 1);
 	}
